"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-08-05T03:13:11Z","updated_at":"2025-08-05T08:19:15Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable (49a5bc7b6) - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2080 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13600K (20 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf you have existing bezier component vector animation tracks (e.g. Node3D position:x and position:y tracks) but are missing one or more vector components (e.g. position:z), there is no way to enable the missing vector component track in the animation without deleting the existing tracks.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Add a Node3D and an AnimationPlayer to a scene\n- Create a new animation and add the Node3D's position as a track using the key icon in the Node3D's inspector panel and choose User Bezier Curves from the dialog\n- Delete one of the track components\n- Trying to add the vector component animation track in any way doesn't work\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp-vector-component-animation-track.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21589227/mrp-vector-component-animation-track.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109321/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0